Inbound SimpleX attachments reached the gateway as unreadable paths.

simplex-chat reports fileSource.filePath RELATIVE to its --files-folder
(observed against 7.0.0: a received image arrives as "test-image_3.jpg").
The adapter forwarded that string as media_urls; the gateway then resolved
it against its own working directory and dropped the attachment:

    WARNING gateway.run: Native image attachment: skipped 1 unreadable
    path(s): ['test-image_3.jpg']

The agent answered "I don't see any image in this message".

The daemon does not tell its websocket clients where --files-folder is,
so the deployment must: the adapter reads SIMPLEX_FILES_FOLDER (set by
the hermes guest module next to SIMPLEX_WS_URL) and resolves relative
paths against it. Absolute paths and unset env pass through unchanged.

--- a/platforms/simplex/adapter.py
+++ b/platforms/simplex/adapter.py
@@ -67,6 +67,19 @@
     return ext.lower() in _AUDIO_EXTS
 
 
+def _resolve_file_path(file_path: str) -> str:
+    """Resolve the daemon's relative filePath against SIMPLEX_FILES_FOLDER.
+
+    simplex-chat reports received files relative to its --files-folder;
+    the gateway needs a path readable from ITS working directory.
+    """
+    if file_path and not os.path.isabs(file_path):
+        base = os.environ.get("SIMPLEX_FILES_FOLDER", "")
+        if base:
+            return str(Path(base) / file_path)
+    return file_path
+
